  nonce: ba60  # ba60
  data:  # ba60
    kind: work_item  # ba60
    title: "cuda: a function returning a pointer gets no symbol and every call in it is dropped (_get_function_name descends no pointer_declarator)"  # ba60
    status: todo_hard  # ba60
    priority: 3  # ba60
    parent:  # ba60
    tags:  # ba60
    - cuda  # ba60
    - call_graph  # ba60
    - analysis_quality  # ba60
    isbefore: []  # ba60
    duplicate_of: []  # ba60
    not_duplicate_of: []  # ba60
    pr_ref:  # ba60
    description: "FOUND 2026-10-01 sweeping WI-saduj's mechanism (a definition whose name sits under a pointer_declarator gets no symbol) across the C-family analyzers.\n\ncuda.py `_get_function_name` and `_extract_cuda_signature` look for a `function_declarator` as a DIRECT child of the `function_definition` and descend NO wrapper at all, so every CUDA function returning a pointer gets no symbol and every call inside it is left unemitted. Its final `return None` is marked `# pragma: no cover`, but it is reachable.\n\nRepro (dev 4208070d1d, analyze_cuda_files on a scratch dir with k.cu):\n  __device__ int helper(int x) { return x; }\n  __device__ int plain(int n) { return helper(n); }\n  __device__ float *one_ptr(float *p) { helper(1); return p; }\n  __device__ float **two_ptr(float **p) { helper(2); return p; }\n-> symbols: helper, plain only; calls: one edge (line 2, from plain). one_ptr and two_ptr and the calls on lines 3 and 4 are absent.\n\nFIX SHAPE: the declarator-chain walk WI-saduj adds to c.py (`c_family_declarator`: follow the `declarator` field and the unnamed inner declarator of parenthesized/reference wrappers; the innermost function_declarator is the function's own). lang-common cannot import lang-mainstream, so either move the walk to hypergumbo_core.analyze.base and use it from c, cpp and cuda, or give cuda its own call. Also check glsl.py / hlsl.py (they mention function_declarator; neither language has pointers, so likely unaffected -- NOT checked). Not measured on a corpus repo: no CUDA repo was looked for."  # ba60
    fields: {}  # ba60
- op: discuss  # 6a40
  at: '2026-10-04T22:59:14Z'  # 6a40
  by: agent  # 6a40
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 6a40
  clock: 2  # 6a40
  nonce: 6a40  # 6a40
  message: "Branch jgstern-agent/fix/darik, commits 80ecd183ca (the declarator walk moved from c.py to hypergumbo_core.analyze.c_family, shared by c, cpp and cuda -- it was NOT shared before; lang-common cannot import lang-mainstream) and 3b1313e103 (cuda). NOT merged, no status change.\n\nWhat changed in cuda.py: names come from the shared walk at any declarator depth (pointer, reference, parenthesised) and for every C++ leaf (field_identifier, qualified A::run, operator, destructor, template specialisation); the signature carries one * per pointer level. The caller is found by POSITION (was by name: of two same-named definitions every call went to the last). A macro-named definition (PFX(f)(args)) is stood in for (WI-tikop's rule). cuda now spells edge_type=\"calls\" literally, so test_call_anchor_gate_common enumerates it; it is classified VERIFIED.\n\nLive repro (the filed one): before -- symbols helper, plain; one edge (line 2). After -- helper, plain, one_ptr, two_ptr; edges at lines 2, 3, 4, each src resolves.\n\nMeasured (~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/decontend/run_10032026/darik/*.cuda.*.json): pytorch .cu/.cuh (414 files) definitions without a symbol 594 -> 77 (the 77 are macro-named, now stood in), call edges 15,866 -> 18,292; whisper.cpp 134 -> 0, 4,635 -> 4,784; ffmpeg 2 -> 0, 409 -> 417; vmaf unchanged (124). The filed shape alone (pointer return) held 81 call sites on pytorch and 73 on whisper.cpp; reference returns held 1,371 on pytorch; the rest were C++ leaves. glsl.py / hlsl.py read a direct-child function_declarator; neither language has pointer or reference declarators -- read, not measured.\n\nResidual filed: WI-fidih-salal-pipoj-tasuh-diguf-jarit-sijuf-vutum (file-scope calls; member/qualified/template callees)."  # 6a40
